Error [E0056]: `mut` is now the `&` sigil
  --> tests/ui/two_capability_markers.jet:3:9
    |
  3 | fn bump(mut x: &Int) {
    |         ^^^
 Why: capability is written with a sigil on the type, not a word — so all code reads the same
 Fix: write `&` in place of `mut`

Error [E0029]: `x` has two capability markers
  --> tests/ui/two_capability_markers.jet:3:13
    |
  3 | fn bump(mut x: &Int) {
    |             ^
 Why: a parameter's access capability is written once — on the type (`name: &Type`), or on `self` for a receiver
 Fix: keep the sigil on the type and remove the other
